sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch14-10> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-10--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-10--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch14-10: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.32" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.32"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "needs-new-data" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.5"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Gradual acquisition would be testable if comparable cognitive scores existed across a phylogeny, and they do not exist as a public dataset. Scattered experiments and endocranial volumes cover a few faculties in a few clades and leave 'each mental power' unmeasured. Until those scores are collected on a common scale, the analysis cannot confirm or refute the claim." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: On a phylogenetic tree, score each mental capacity on a common ordinal scale across animals and humans and test whether every capacity appears by intermediate stages rather than in a single jump. The claim is confirmed if each capacity has precursor states in related organisms or in the archaeological and fossil record, and refuted by a capacity whose first appearance has no structural or behavioral intermediate." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Mental capacities are not measured on one scale across taxa, so published experiments cannot be stacked into a single analysis.", "A missing intermediate can always be assigned to an untested or extinct species, which weakens refutation.", "Brain-size and archaeological records do not resolve particular faculties such as language or abstraction." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-10--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch14-10 by Grok 4.7: 0.45" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.45"^^xsd:double ;
